<title>USA: U.S. mortgage application volume fell in latest wk.</title>
<headline>U.S. mortgage application volume fell in latest wk.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The volume of U.S. mortgage applications fell 23.6 percent in the week ended May 30, according to a Mortgage Bankers Association of America weekly survey.</p>
<p>Specifically, the volume of applications to refinance mortgages fell 27.3 percent in the latest survey week, while applications to purchase mortgages decreased 22.6 percent.</p>
<p>The seasonally adjusted refinancing index fell 9.1 percent to 295.6 from 325.1 the previous week.</p>
<p>The purchase index slipped 2.0 percent to 187.2 in the latest survey from 191.1 in the previous week  </p>
